# [BENCHMARK] Task: E-Commerce Ticket Data Extraction & Schema Optimization

> **Goal:** Test whether free LLMs can parse customer complaints into strict, machine-readable JSON without formatting errors or conversational text.

---

## 1. Test Setup

* **Model Tested:** Gemini 1.5 Flash (via Google AI Studio)
* **Raw User Input:**
  > "HEY! I bought two black winter jackets (Order #88392) last Tuesday. One of them arrived with a broken zipper! I tried calling but no one answered. I want a replacement for the broken jacket ASAP or I'm canceling my subscription! Contact me at alex99@email.com."

---

## 2. Iterative Schema Development

During testing, the JSON output went through three iterations to move from basic extraction to an API-ready standard:

### Iteration 1 (Baseline Output)
* Unstructured strings and missing numerical counts.
* Used string flags for risk factors (`"cancellation_risk": "yes"`).

### Iteration 2 (Final Schema)
```json
{
  "order_number": "88392",
  "product_details": "black winter jacket",
  "damaged_units": 1,
  "stock_units": 1,
  "emergency_level": "high",
  "cancellation_risk": true,
  "contact_email": "alex99@email.com",
  "important_points": [
    "broken zipper reported",
    "customer requested replacement",
    "unsuccessful phone support attempt",
    "urgent resolution required"
  ]
}
